HYP-2696 / T932 -- LRC14 Bonferroni4 transfer tax
Arithmetic: exact Fractions over HYP-2691 common sector-wall refinements.
Preserved predicate: p0(E) <= U4(E), with U4(E)=p0+p5+5p6.
Assumption challenged: proof vertices are missed-state transitions and schedules, not runners.

EXACT LOCAL LAW
  For every insertion P -> P union {e}:
    Delta U4 = mass(1->0) - mass(5->4) - 4*mass(6->5).
  Positive Bonferroni4 movement is exactly one-missed closure;
  five/six-missed transitions are a signed tax that lowers U4.

