SYNTHESIS
  The transfer law is exact on every audited row and schedule.
  Boundary/AP rows can fail the final U4 gate because their high tail
  survives as finite template mass.  True-wide rows in the bank have
  enough transfer tax to keep U4 below cap after the same p0 closures.
  New proof target: classify or bound the possible unpaid 1->0 closures
  after the 5->4 and 6->5 high-tail tax has been exhausted.
